+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Columns may be reordered. Tickets are nonempty strings, soldAt is an ISO
+  instant with a timezone, dishId identifies a dish, and qty is a positive
+  whole number of portions. Returns `{ "tickets": 1, "dishes": 2 }` (new
+  tickets and total portions imported). Previously imported tickets are
+  skipped; repeated rows of a new ticket are all imported. All rows are
+  validated, including skipped tickets. Any failure rejects the whole file
+  with a row-numbered error (first data row is row 2). Ingredient movements
+  use the sale instant and ref `sale:<ticket>`.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 0.6, "actual": 0.8, "variance": 0.2 }`
+  sorted by item id. Days are inclusive in UTC; from must not exceed to.
+  Theoretical use is the saved ingredient quantities of imported sales;
+  actual use includes every consume movement. Variance is actual minus
+  theoretical. Items with neither use are omitted.
